---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { CAREERS_HREF, COMPANY, COMPANY_ADDRESS, ENQUIRE_HREF, SITE } from '@/data/site'

/** Shown at the top of the policy; change it whenever the wording below changes. */
const LAST_UPDATED = '9 November 2026'

const site = Astro.site ?? new URL('https://flairentertainment.je')
const privacyPage = {
	'@type': 'WebPage',
	name: 'Privacy policy',
	url: new URL('/privacy/', site).href,
	about: { '@id': `${site.href}#organization` },
}
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Privacy Policy"
	description="How Flair Entertainment Limited collects, uses and protects the personal data you send through this website, and your rights under the Data Protection (Jersey) Law 2018."
	schema={[privacyPage]}
>
	<section class="intro section">
		<p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
		<h1 class="display">Privacy <span class="script still">policy</span></h1>
		<div class="lede">
			<p>How we look after the details you share with us.</p>
			<p>Last updated {LAST_UPDATED}</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<article class="policy section">
		<section>
			<h2 class="title">Who we are</h2>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>
					This website is run by {COMPANY.legalName}, a private company registered in {COMPANY.jurisdiction} under company number
					{COMPANY.registrationNumber}, with its registered office at {COMPANY_ADDRESS}. We trade as {SITE.name}.
				</p>
				<p>
					We are the data controller for the personal data described here, which means we decide how and why it is used. We handle it in line with
					the Data Protection (Jersey) Law 2018.
				</p>
				<p>
					For any question about this policy or your data, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> or write to us at our
					registered office.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="title">What we collect and why</h2>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>We only collect what you choose to send us.</p>
				<h3>Booking enquiries</h3>
				<p>
					When you use the <a href={ENQUIRE_HREF}>enquiry form</a> we receive your first and last name, your email address, your event date if you
					give one, and your message. We use them to reply, to put a proposal together and, if you go ahead, to arrange and deliver your event. We
					rely on the fact that you have asked us to take these steps before entering into a contract, and on our legitimate interest in answering
					the people who contact us.
				</p>
				<h3>Performer applications</h3>
				<p>
					When you apply through the <a href={CAREERS_HREF}>careers form</a> we receive your name, email address, phone number, location, the
					disciplines you tick, your training, genre and skills, your portfolio or showreel link, your social media handle and your message. We use
					them to consider you for work and to contact you about it. We rely on our legitimate interest in finding performers, and on the steps you
					have asked us to take before any engagement.
				</p>
				<h3>Emails and calls</h3>
				<p>
					If you email or phone us directly, we use your contact details and what you tell us to deal with your message, on the same basis as the
					forms above.
				</p>
				<h3>Visiting the site</h3>
				<p>
					Like any web host, our hosting provider records technical details of each visit, such as your IP address, browser and the page requested,
					so it can deliver the site and protect it from abuse. This is in our legitimate interest in running a secure website. We do not use these
					records to identify you.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="title">Cookies and tracking</h2>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>
					This website sets no cookies. It has no analytics, advertising or social media tracking, and it loads nothing from other companies'
					servers: the fonts, images and video are served from our own host.
				</p>
				<p>
					The only thing it keeps in your browser is a single flag in session storage that records that the site's fonts have loaded, so later pages
					don't wait for them again. It holds no personal data, is never sent to us, and your browser deletes it when you close the tab.
				</p>
				<p>
					Our Instagram and Facebook links take you to those services, whose own privacy policies apply once you are there.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="title">Who handles your data</h2>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>
					This website is hosted by Netlify, Inc., a company based in the United States. Netlify stores the messages sent through our forms on our
					behalf and passes them to us. Because of this, your details are processed outside Jersey. Netlify acts only on our instructions under its
					data processing terms, which include contractual safeguards for international transfers.
				</p>
				<p>
					Messages also reach our email provider so the team can read and answer them. Apart from these service providers, we share your details only
					where you have asked us to or where the law requires it. We do not sell personal data.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="title">How long we keep it</h2>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>
					We keep enquiries for up to two years after our last contact with you, so we can pick up where we left off if you come back to us. Where
					an enquiry becomes a booking, we keep the records we need for as long as Jersey accounting and tax law requires.
				</p>
				<p>
					We keep performer applications for up to twelve months so we can consider you for work that comes up. If you join our roster, we keep
					your details for as long as we work together. You can ask us to delete an application sooner at any time.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="title">Your rights</h2>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>Under the Data Protection (Jersey) Law 2018 you have the right to:</p>
				<ul>
					<li>ask for a copy of the personal data we hold about you</li>
					<li>have inaccurate or incomplete data corrected</li>
					<li>have your data erased</li>
					<li>restrict how we use your data</li>
					<li>object to our use of your data where we rely on legitimate interests</li>
					<li>receive data you gave us in a portable format, or have it sent to someone else</li>
					<li>withdraw your consent at any time, where we rely on it</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					To use any of these rights, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. There is no charge. We may need to confirm who
					you are before we act, and we will reply within four weeks, or tell you within that time if the law allows us longer because the request is
					complex.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="title">Complaints</h2>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>
					If you are unhappy with how we have handled your data, please tell us first so we can put it right. You also have the right to complain to
					the Jersey Office of the Information Commissioner, the island's data protection regulator, at
					<a href="https://jerseyoic.org" rel="noopener">jerseyoic.org</a>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="title">Changes to this policy</h2>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>
					We will update this page if the way we handle personal data changes. The date at the top shows when it was last revised.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.intro {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 36px;
		padding-block: 160px 96px;
		text-align: center;
	}

	.policy {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 64px;
		max-width: calc(720px + 2 * var(--gutter));
		margin-inline: auto;
		padding-bottom: 160px;
	}

	.policy section {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 24px;
	}

	.policy h3 {
		margin-top: 8px;
		margin-bottom: -12px;
		font: 600 10px/1.6 var(--font-sans);
		letter-spacing: 0.3em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--ink);
	}

	.policy ul {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 6px;
		padding-left: 20px;
		list-style: disc;
	}

	.policy a {
		border-bottom: 1px solid currentColor;
		color: var(--ink);
	}

	@media (max-width: 700px) {
		.intro {
			gap: 24px;
			padding-block: 72px 56px;
		}

		.policy {
			gap: 48px;
			padding-bottom: 96px;
		}
	}
</style>
